{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014qdVdvMrojbjsczw8vNhQm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# LRUCache spec\n2\t\n3\t`LRUCache(capacity: int, ttl: float | None = None, clock=time.monotonic)`\n4\t\n5\t- `get(key, default=None)`: return the value and mark the key as most recently used.\n6\t  Expired entries behave as missing and are removed.\n7\t- `put(key, value)`: insert or update; updating also marks as most recently used.\n8\t  When the cache is over capacity, evict the least recently used entry.\n9\t- `delete(key) -> bool`: remove, return whether it existed.\n10\t- `__len__`, `__contains__` (contains must not change recency, must respect TTL).\n11\t- `stats()` returns `{\"hits\": int, \"misses\": int, \"evictions\": int, \"expirations\": int}`.\n12\t  Expired entries count as a miss and an expiration, not an eviction.\n13\t- `capacity <= 0` raises `ValueError`.\n14\t- All operations O(1) average. Use `collections.OrderedDict`.\n15\t- `clock` is injectable for tests; TTL is measured with it.\n16\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33d74e14-44a2-4145-9ef3-07addb5871cc","uuid":"ba458bce-120a-4b67-a7d5-a7c1463cf9c0","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:01:39.533Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-sonnet-5-5-effort-low/cases/t04_lru_cache/cachelib/SPEC.md","content":"# LRUCache spec\n\n`LRUCache(capacity: int, ttl: float | None = None, clock=time.monotonic)`\n\n- `get(key, default=None)`: return the value and mark the key as most recently used.\n  Expired entries behave as missing and are removed.\n- `put(key, value)`: insert or update; updating also marks as most recently used.\n  When the cache is over capacity, evict the least recently used entry.\n- `delete(key) -> bool`: remove, return whether it existed.\n- `__len__`, `__contains__` (contains must not change recency, must respect TTL).\n- `stats()` returns `{\"hits\": int, \"misses\": int, \"evictions\": int, \"expirations\": int}`.\n  Expired entries count as a miss and an expiration, not an eviction.\n- `capacity <= 0` raises `ValueError`.\n- All operations O(1) average. Use `collections.OrderedDict`.\n- `clock` is injectable for tests; TTL is measured with it.\n","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":16}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014qdVdvMrojbjsczw8vNhQm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
