{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrwhdwiTon2Z3jY9khe7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented `cachelib/lru.py` to the spec and added `tests/test_lru.py`. All 9 tests pass.\n\nThe tests use an injected fake clock and cover:\n- the `capacity <= 0` error\n- get and put, including the default value\n- eviction order\n- an update refreshing recency\n- `__contains__` leaving recency alone\n- delete\n- TTL expiry through both `get` and `in`\n- `put` resetting the TTL\n\nTwo behaviors the spec doesn't settle, which I chose:\n- **Expiry boundary:** an entry expires when `now >= put_time + ttl`, so it is already gone exactly at the TTL.\n- **`len()` and expired entries:** `len()` is O(1) and counts stored entries, so an expired entry that nobody has read yet still counts until `get` or `in` removes it. Purging in `len()` would make it O(n).\n\n`in` also removes an expired entry and counts an expiration. It doesn't count a miss, since the spec only defines misses for `get`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13762,"cache_read_input_tokens":23122,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13762},"output_tokens":334,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33d74e14-44a2-4145-9ef3-07addb5871cc","uuid":"97b7d594-3f1d-4a1c-b7dd-d40f9aecaf57","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:01:57.442Z","request_id":"req_011Cfrwhdh5RdxoRA6sCnHeb"}
